“I can’t understand how that’s possible, because if you ask people, nobody wants a war, so how does it happen?
Ten years is nothing with such pain.
We need dozens of years to forget it a little bit.
It's attacked my health and I'm still feeling it.
For about three or four years I've had a few nightmares because of the siege, but then it got better.
I went back to school later in 2004 and was scared every day.
I thought of my friends and classmates who had been killed.
That's why I always go to the sports hall as September 1 is approaching.
I'm trying to pay tribute to my old childhood friends.
