I don't feel as a victim, this story is now a part of my past.
I won't forget, but I don't feel sorry.
My life continues.
I graduated school this year and attend a medical college in Vladikawkaz.
I'm going to be a heart surgeon.
My first choice was training in the army.
I wanted to become a soldier, but my health didn't allow it.
I wanted to fight for my country, but that won't happen.
Georgy Faniyev, 20
The boy who survived even though he was trapped at the feat of a murderous terrorist
