Makhar, then three years old, escaped, but Aljona's mother and sister died in the murderous carnage.
Her father Ruslan has remarried since then and with his new wife Svetlana a little gill that he named Kristina after his lost daughter.
Aljona, now ten years old, doesn't remember the siege and has grown into an intelligent and happy girl, neighbors say.
"They're a big happy family now and Aljona and Makhar are both great kids," says a close friend.
Ruslan is a fantastic father and wants to spare them all the memories coming up with the 10th anniversary.
You'll understand why.
Man accuses assaulting girl on pedestrian crossing in Fife
